Design Decisions
Architecture

The project follows a simple controller pattern, separating the main menu flow (Program.cs) from the business logic (PetController.cs). Each entity has its own file following C# conventions.

In-memory storage

Data is stored in a List<Pet> held in memory for the duration of the program session. There is no database integration — this was an intentional decision to keep the scope focused on OOP and C# fundamentals. A future version could integrate Entity Framework Core and SQL Server.

Input validation

Most inputs are validated using int.TryParse and DateTime.TryParse with loop-based retry logic. Some fields (vaccination name, procedure name) do not have full validation — this was a deliberate trade-off to keep the project moving forward, and is documented here as a known limitation.

Encapsulation

All entity properties use { get; private set; }. Mutation is only allowed through dedicated methods (EditarNome, EditarEspecie, EditarIdade) on the Pet class, keeping data modification controlled and intentional.

